Package: ggsmartext
Title: Smart Axis Labels for 'ggplot2'
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R:
    person("JunJun", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "junjun@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: A smart axis labelling system for 'ggplot2'. When a
    discrete x or y axis carries too many category labels, the guide
    implemented here displays only the labels the user asks for, packs
    the remaining space with leader lines that connect each displayed
    label to its tick, and distributes the labels over several rows (or
    columns) so that the available page space is used efficiently. The
    one-dimensional, overlap-free arrangement is a port of the
    'smartAlign' algorithm used by the 'circlize' package and of the
    box arrangement used by the 'ComplexHeatmap' package.
